<p>This looks like a ton of ingredients, but a lot of them are pantry items=
 that I bet you already have on hand. We=E2=80=99re talking spices, nutriti=
onal yeast, arrowroot powder, cornmeal, Dijon mustard, maple syrup, olive o=
il, Tamari soy sauce, and white wine vinegar. A lot of my go-to=E2=80=99s! =
In terms of prep, we blend the dressing, roast the sweet potatoes and <a hr=
ef=3D"https://thefirstmess.com/2022/10/26/crispy-baked-tofu-bits/">crispy b=
aked tofu</a>, massage the kale in some olive oil and lime juice, and then =
assemble.</p>



<p>The dressing is truly the real winner of this recipe though. It=E2=80=99=
s spicy, tangy, savoury, creamy, and so delicious. I make a double batch an=
d use it on grain bowls, to finish tacos, drizzled over crispy air fried br=
occoli, as a dip for fresh veg, and all kinds of salads.</p>



<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading">Some Tips for Making This Kale Power Salad:<=
/h2>



<ul class=3D"wp-block-list">
<li>You can substitute raw sunflower seeds or cashews for the almonds.&nbsp=
;</li>



<li>Use the biggest baking sheet you=E2=80=99ve got for the sweet potatoes =
and tofu. You want to give each piece as much space as you can!</li>



<li>You will find yourself wanting to put this dressing on everything. I do=
uble up on this one.</li>
</ul>



<p>If you=E2=80=99re a fan of this salad, you=E2=80=99ll probably love my <=
a href=3D"https://thefirstmess.com/2023/09/27/kale-sweet-potato-salad-chick=
peas-spicy-tahini-ranch/">Sweet Potato Kale Salad</a>, <a href=3D"https://t=
hefirstmess.com/2021/10/15/apple-kale-salad-miso-mustard-dressing/">Chopped=
 Apple, Kale &amp; Parsnip Salad</a> or my <a href=3D"https://thefirstmess.=
com/2021/07/07/vegan-kale-cobb-salad/">Vegan Kale Cobb Salad</a>. You might=
 also like this roundup of <a href=3D"https://thefirstmess.com/2021/08/11/s=
weet-potato-recipes/">Sweet Potato Recipes</a>.</p>



